[{:db/id 17592186362391 :question/problem "Consider the following set of functions:\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{f}_{2}(t)={sin}^{2}⁡t,\\,{f}_{3}(t)=1\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space $C[0,\\pi ]$ of continuous functions over $[0,\\pi ]$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨f(t),g(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(t)g(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nII. ${f}_{2}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nIII. $S=\\{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product\n\n*Hint: $⟨{f}_{1},{f}_{2}⟩=0.$*" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186362392 :question/problem "Consider the following set of functions:\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=1,\\,{f}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{f}_{3}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space $C[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ of continuous functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨f(t),g(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(t)g(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nII. ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nIII. $S=\\{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product\n\n*Hint: $⟨{f}_{2},{f}_{3}⟩=0$*" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186237782 :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=t-2,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t+2,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=2t+4.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-2)q(-2)+p(2)q(2),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nII. ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nIII. $S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186380393 :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t-4,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=2-t,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=1-t.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(1)q(1)+p(2)q(2),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nII. ${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nIII. $S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186380406 :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t+2,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t-2,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=t+1.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(2)q(2),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nII. ${p}_{2}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nIII. $S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-024faa8c-8ac3-506b-9b2c-333430674981" :activity/id #uuid "024faa8c-8ac3-506b-9b2c-333430674981" :activity/title "Orthogonal Sets in Inner Product Spaces" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048572 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-7f2a99f1-09d3-5682-bc31-b6d8c58eeab4" "step-0052f793-89f1-5c58-93a6-48098b6aceba" "step-7719daea-6d1b-5000-8b05-8e73d08e6429" "step-246bcb3d-ab36-5471-897e-d2a54e64c4f2" "step-f46df5aa-3941-5c4e-8920-7488094bbef3"] :activity/first-step "ste